[{"pressReleaseTitle":"Reinstatement of AT1 Bonds Credit Neutral for Yes Bank","effectiveDate":"Oct 23, 2026 | Yes Bank Ltd","overview":"<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">India Ratings and research (Ind-Ra) opines the Supreme Court’s order\r\ndirecting the reinstatement of Yes Bank Limited’s (YBL; debt rated at </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\r\nmso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:\r\nEN-US;mso-bidi-language:AR-SA\"><a href=\"https://www.indiaratings.co.in/pressrelease/84853\"><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">IND\r\nAA+/Stable</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size:9.0pt;line-height:115%;\r\nfont-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-ansi-language:EN-US;mso-fareast-language:EN-US;mso-bidi-language:\r\nAR-SA\">) Additional Tier 1 (AT1) bonds as credit neutral in the near term. This\r\nis because Ind-Ra believes YBL has potential capital management levers which\r\nwill keep its pro forma CET1 ratio above its negative rating sensitivity for\r\nCET-1 of 12%. Furthermore, Ind-Ra believes YBL has the ability to raise equity\r\ncapital, supported by the presence of Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation\r\n(SMBC) as its largest shareholder, along with the improvement in the bank’s\r\nfinancial performance over the past few years. Given YBL’s strategic importance\r\nto SMBC, Ind-Ra expects shareholder support to remain available, if required.<br><br></span></p>","thumbNailImagePath":null,"primaryAnalystName":"Krushabh Naik"}]